IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `tas-nouns`

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1931 (Tasmania), ss 24 to 28: references, writing, printing, documents, number, derivatives, genders, Ministers, officers, this State, distance.
-- Answers of a rule of reading: JUST TRUE where the text applies to the case; JUST FALSE only where the text itself says no to the case in its own words
--   (a "means" definition, a condition introduced with "if", "only if", "as long as" or "unless", a list closed with "only", a flat negative, a "where" that fails, a period the text fixes and the case falls outside it);
-- NOTHING everywhere else (an open list, "includes", a term left undefined, silence, a pointer outside the sources, a grant or prohibition limited by its own wording where the case falls outside the limit, a scope limit with no "only").
-- A rule that returns a day, a name or a value has no second not-covered answer, so it returns NOTHING when its text does not apply.
-- s 24(c) is shown only as a row of dots and is not encoded.

§ `s 24: construction of certain references, expressions and words`

-- src:545 | (a) references to the Sovereign reigning at the time of the passing of that Act, or to the Crown, shall be construed as references to the Sovereign for the time being;
@ref s 24(a) (src:545)
GIVEN `the reference is in an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reference is to the Sovereign reigning at the time of the passing of that Act, or to the Crown` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 24(a): the reference is construed as a reference to the Sovereign for the time being` `the reference is in an Act` `the reference is to the Sovereign reigning at the time of the passing of that Act, or to the Crown` MEANS
    IF `the reference is in an Act` AND `the reference is to the Sovereign reigning at the time of the passing of that Act, or to the Crown`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:547 | (b) expressions referring to writing shall be construed as including references to any mode of representing or reproducing words, figures, or symbols in a visible form;
@ref s 24(b) (src:547)
GIVEN `the expression is in an Act and refers to writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the mode represents or reproduces words, figures or symbols in a visible form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 24(b): the expression includes a reference to the mode` `the expression is in an Act and refers to writing` `the mode represents or reproduces words, figures or symbols in a visible form` MEANS
    IF `the expression is in an Act and refers to writing` AND `the mode represents or reproduces words, figures or symbols in a visible form`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Means of reproducing writing` IS ONE OF
    `typewriting`
    `lithography`
    `any mechanical means`
    `any electrical means`
    `any electronic means`
    `some other means`

-- src:549 | (ba) expressions referring to printing shall be construed as including references to typewriting and writing reproduced by lithography or by any mechanical, electrical or electronic means;
@ref s 24(ba) (src:549)
GIVEN `the expression is in an Act and refers to printing` IS A BOOLEAN
      means IS A `Means of reproducing writing`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 24(ba): the expression includes a reference to` `the expression is in an Act and refers to printing` means MEANS
    IF `the expression is in an Act and refers to printing` AND NOT (means EQUALS `some other means`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:551 | (bb) references to a document shall be construed as including references to –
-- src:553 | (i) any paper or other material on which there is printing or writing or on which there are marks, symbols, or perforations having a meaning for persons qualified to interpret them; and
-- src:555 | (ii) a disc, tape, or other article from which sounds, images, writing, or messages are capable of being reproduced; and
@ref s 24(bb) (src:551-555)
GIVEN `the reference is in an Act and is to a document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is paper or other material on which there is printing or writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is paper or other material on which there are marks, symbols or perforations having a meaning for persons qualified to interpret them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is a disc, tape or other article from which sounds, images, writing or messages are capable of being reproduced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 24(bb): the reference includes a reference to the thing` `the reference is in an Act and is to a document` `the thing is paper or other material on which there is printing or writing` `the thing is paper or other material on which there are marks, symbols or perforations having a meaning for persons qualified to interpret them` `the thing is a disc, tape or other article from which sounds, images, writing or messages are capable of being reproduced` MEANS
    IF `the reference is in an Act and is to a document` AND (`the thing is paper or other material on which there is printing or writing` OR `the thing is paper or other material on which there are marks, symbols or perforations having a meaning for persons qualified to interpret them` OR `the thing is a disc, tape or other article from which sounds, images, writing or messages are capable of being reproduced`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:559 | (d) words in the singular shall include the plural and words in the plural shall include the singular –
-- src:561 | and where any word is defined every derivative of that word shall have a meaning corresponding with such definition.
@ref s 24(d) (src:559-561)
GIVEN form IS A `Number form of a word`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Number form of a word`
`s 24(d): a word in the number form includes` form MEANS
    CONSIDER form
    WHEN `the singular` THEN LIST `the singular`, `the plural`
    WHEN `the plural` THEN LIST `the plural`, `the singular`

-- src:541 | 24. Construction of certain references, expressions, and words
-- src:543 | In any Act –
-- src:545 | (a) references to the Sovereign reigning at the time of the passing of that Act, or to the Crown, shall be construed as references to the Sovereign for the time being;
-- src:547 | (b) expressions referring to writing shall be construed as including references to any mode of representing or reproducing words, figures, or symbols in a visible form;
-- src:549 | (ba) expressions referring to printing shall be construed as including references to typewriting and writing reproduced by lithography or by any mechanical, electrical or electronic means;
-- src:551 | (bb) references to a document shall be construed as including references to –
-- src:553 | (i) any paper or other material on which there is printing or writing or on which there are marks, symbols, or perforations having a meaning for persons qualified to interpret them; and
-- src:555 | (ii) a disc, tape, or other article from which sounds, images, writing, or messages are capable of being reproduced; and
-- src:557 | (c) . . . . . . . .
-- src:559 | (d) words in the singular shall include the plural and words in the plural shall include the singular –
-- src:561 | and where any word is defined every derivative of that word shall have a meaning corresponding with such definition.
@ref s 24 derivatives (src:541-561)
GIVEN `the word is defined in an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other word is a derivative of the defined word` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 24: the derivative has a meaning corresponding with the definition` `the word is defined in an Act` `the other word is a derivative of the defined word` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`the word is defined in an Act`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- a failed "where"
           IF NOT (`the other word is a derivative of the defined word`) THEN NOTHING   -- a scope limit with no "only"
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

#ASSERT `s 24(a): the reference is construed as a reference to the Sovereign for the time being` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 24(a): the reference is construed as a reference to the Sovereign for the time being` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 24(a): the reference is construed as a reference to the Sovereign for the time being` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 24(b): the expression includes a reference to the mode` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 24(b): the expression includes a reference to the mode` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 24(b): the expression includes a reference to the mode` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 24(ba): the expression includes a reference to` TRUE `typewriting` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 24(ba): the expression includes a reference to` TRUE `lithography` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 24(ba): the expression includes a reference to` TRUE `any mechanical means` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 24(ba): the expression includes a reference to` TRUE `any electrical means` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 24(ba): the expression includes a reference to` TRUE `any electronic means` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 24(ba): the expression includes a reference to` TRUE `some other means` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 24(ba): the expression includes a reference to` FALSE `typewriting` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 24(bb): the reference includes a reference to the thing` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 24(bb): the reference includes a reference to the thing` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 24(bb): the reference includes a reference to the thing` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 24(bb): the reference includes a reference to the thing` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 24(bb): the reference includes a reference to the thing` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT elem `the plural` (`s 24(d): a word in the number form includes` `the singular`)
#ASSERT elem `the singular` (`s 24(d): a word in the number form includes` `the singular`)
#ASSERT elem `the singular` (`s 24(d): a word in the number form includes` `the plural`)
#ASSERT elem `the plural` (`s 24(d): a word in the number form includes` `the plural`)
#ASSERT `s 24: the derivative has a meaning corresponding with the definition` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 24: the derivative has a meaning corresponding with the definition` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 24: the derivative has a meaning corresponding with the definition` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 24A: genders`

-- src:565 | (1) A word or expression that indicates one or more particular genders is taken to include every other gender.
@ref s 24A(1) (src:565)
GIVEN `the genders the word or expression indicates` IS A LIST OF `Gender`
      gender IS A `Gender`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 24A(1): the word or expression is taken to include the gender` `the genders the word or expression indicates` gender MEANS
    CONSIDER `the genders the word or expression indicates`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN g FOLLOWED BY rest THEN JUST TRUE

-- src:567 | (2) A word in either the masculine or feminine gender includes a body corporate or unincorporate.
@ref s 24A(2) (src:567)
GIVEN gender IS A `Gender`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 24A(2): a word in the gender includes a body corporate or unincorporate` gender MEANS
    CONSIDER gender
    WHEN `the masculine gender` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the feminine gender` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a gender other than masculine or feminine` THEN NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 24A(1): the word or expression is taken to include the gender` (LIST `the masculine gender`) `the feminine gender` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 24A(1): the word or expression is taken to include the gender` (LIST `the feminine gender`) `a gender other than masculine or feminine` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 24A(1): the word or expression is taken to include the gender` (LIST `the masculine gender`, `the feminine gender`) `a gender other than masculine or feminine` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 24A(1): the word or expression is taken to include the gender` (LIST `a gender other than masculine or feminine`) `the masculine gender` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 24A(1): the word or expression is taken to include the gender` (EMPTY) `the masculine gender` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 24A(2): a word in the gender includes a body corporate or unincorporate` `the masculine gender` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 24A(2): a word in the gender includes a body corporate or unincorporate` `the feminine gender` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 24A(2): a word in the gender includes a body corporate or unincorporate` `a gender other than masculine or feminine` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 25: references to Minister`

-- src:569 | 25. References to Minister
-- src:571 | Where in any Act any Minister is referred to, such reference, unless the contrary intention appears, shall be deemed to include any Minister for the time being acting for and on behalf of such Minister.
@ref s 25 (src:569-571)
GIVEN `a Minister is referred to in an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other Minister is for the time being acting for and on behalf of that Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25: the reference is deemed to include the other Minister` `a Minister is referred to in an Act` `the contrary intention appears` `the other Minister is for the time being acting for and on behalf of that Minister` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`a Minister is referred to in an Act`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- a failed "Where"
           IF `the contrary intention appears` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `the other Minister is for the time being acting for and on behalf of that Minister` THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 25: the reference is deemed to include the other Minister` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 25: the reference is deemed to include the other Minister` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 25: the reference is deemed to include the other Minister` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 25: the reference is deemed to include the other Minister` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 26: references to an officer in general terms`

-- src:573 | 26. References to an officer in general terms
-- src:575 | Where in any Act reference is made in general terms to any person holding a particular office or position, such reference shall be deemed to include all persons who at any time occupy for the time being such office or position.
@ref s 26 (src:573-575)
GIVEN `reference is made in an Act in general terms to any person holding a particular office or position` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person occupies that office or position for the time being at some time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 26: the reference is deemed to include the person` `reference is made in an Act in general terms to any person holding a particular office or position` `the person occupies that office or position for the time being at some time` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`reference is made in an Act in general terms to any person holding a particular office or position`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- a failed "Where"
           IF NOT (`the person occupies that office or position for the time being at some time`) THEN NOTHING   -- "deemed to include": a scope limit with no "only"
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

#ASSERT `s 26: the reference is deemed to include the person` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 26: the reference is deemed to include the person` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 26: the reference is deemed to include the person` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 27: references to particular officers and the like`

DECLARE `Thing referred to in an Act` IS ONE OF
    `an officer or office`
    `an employee, position or appointment`
    `a locality, jurisdiction or other matter or thing`
    `anything else`

DECLARE `Connection to this State` IS ONE OF
    `in and for this State`
    `in and of this State`

-- src:581 | (a) references to any officer or office shall be construed as references to such officer or office in and for this State;
-- src:583 | (ab) references to any employee, position or appointment shall be construed as references to such employee, position or appointment in and for this State; and
-- src:585 | (b) references to localities, jurisdictions, and other matters and things shall be construed as references to such localities, jurisdictions, and other matters and things in and of this State.
@ref s 27 (src:581-585)
GIVEN thing IS A `Thing referred to in an Act`
GIVETH A MAYBE (`Connection to this State`)
`s 27: the reference is construed as a reference to such a thing` thing MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `an officer or office` THEN JUST `in and for this State`
    WHEN `an employee, position or appointment` THEN JUST `in and for this State`
    WHEN `a locality, jurisdiction or other matter or thing` THEN JUST `in and of this State`
    WHEN `anything else` THEN NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 27: the reference is construed as a reference to such a thing` `an officer or office` EQUALS JUST `in and for this State`
#ASSERT `s 27: the reference is construed as a reference to such a thing` `an employee, position or appointment` EQUALS JUST `in and for this State`
#ASSERT `s 27: the reference is construed as a reference to such a thing` `a locality, jurisdiction or other matter or thing` EQUALS JUST `in and of this State`
#ASSERT `s 27: the reference is construed as a reference to such a thing` `anything else` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 28: measurement of distance`

-- A place is given by two horizontal coordinates and a height.
-- The Act measures the distance "in a straight line on a horizontal plane", so the height does not enter the distance.
DECLARE `Place` HAS
    `metres east` IS A NUMBER
    `metres north` IS A NUMBER
    `metres of height` IS A NUMBER

-- src:587 | 28. Measurement of distance
-- src:589 | In the measurement of any distance for the purposes of any Act, that distance, unless the contrary is expressly provided, shall be measured in a straight line on a horizontal plane.
@ref s 28 (src:587-589)
GIVEN `the distance is measured for the purposes of an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is expressly provided` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 28: the distance is measured in a straight line on a horizontal plane` `the distance is measured for the purposes of an Act` `the contrary is expressly provided` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`the distance is measured for the purposes of an Act`) THEN NOTHING
           IF `the contrary is expressly provided` THEN JUST FALSE
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

GIVEN here IS A `Place`
      there IS A `Place`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 28: the distance in metres, measured in a straight line on a horizontal plane, between` here `and` there MEANS
    SQRT (((here's `metres east`) MINUS (there's `metres east`)) TIMES ((here's `metres east`) MINUS (there's `metres east`)) PLUS ((here's `metres north`) MINUS (there's `metres north`)) TIMES ((here's `metres north`) MINUS (there's `metres north`)))

#ASSERT `s 28: the distance is measured in a straight line on a horizontal plane` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 28: the distance is measured in a straight line on a horizontal plane` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 28: the distance is measured in a straight line on a horizontal plane` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 28: the distance in metres, measured in a straight line on a horizontal plane, between` (`Place` OF 0, 0, 0) `and` (`Place` OF 3, 4, 100) EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `s 28: the distance in metres, measured in a straight line on a horizontal plane, between` (`Place` OF 3, 4, 100) `and` (`Place` OF 0, 0, 0) EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `s 28: the distance in metres, measured in a straight line on a horizontal plane, between` (`Place` OF 10, 10, 0) `and` (`Place` OF 10, 10, 500) EQUALS 0
